# Authentication and security

**Methodology:** [`docs/meta/ai_first_project_methodology.md`](docs/meta/ai_first_project_methodology.md)
**Canon:** [ADR-003](docs/prds/07_governance/adr_003_auth_oidc_jwt_rbac.md) · [`auth_runtime_spec.md`](docs/prds/05_runtime/auth_runtime_spec.md) · [`authorization_matrix.md`](docs/prds/04_authorization_privacy/authorization_matrix.md)
**Guide:** [`docs/guidelines/auth/ai_auth_implementation_guide.md`](docs/guidelines/auth/ai_auth_implementation_guide.md)
**Telegram workarounds:** [`telegram_authjs_oidc_portable_guide.md`](docs/my_specs/telegram_authjs_oidc_portable_guide.md) §6
**Schema:** [`database_schema_v1.md`](docs/prds/03_data_model/database_schema_v1.md) §5.1
**Runtime:** [ADR-002](docs/prds/07_governance/adr_002_nextjs_vercel_runtime_policy.md) — Next.js **16.4** (exact patch pin), **`proxy.ts`**

## Auth model (MVP)

- Sign-in: **Telegram (OIDC)** for everyone; **email + password (Credentials) for administrators only** (ADR-003 v1.1). No Google, no self-registration by password, no password reset in the app, no email-link.
- Sessions: Auth.js v5 `strategy: "jwt"`, **no database adapter**. Identities live in `login_identity`, users in `app_user`.
- Roles: `admin`, `teacher` (from `@sunschool/domain`). Status: `REGISTRATION` → `REQUEST_PENDING` → `ACTIVE` | `REJECTED` | `DISABLED` | `DELETED`.
- Linking a second provider: **signed link-intent cookie** + client `signIn()` — not an adapter (`auth_runtime_spec` §7).

## Layers (defense in depth)

| Layer | Where | What | Must not |
|-------|-------|------|----------|
| 1 | **`proxy.ts`** via `auth.config.ts` + `@sunschool/policy-edge` | Optimistic redirect by JWT `status` / path prefix | import `auth.ts`, `@sunschool/db`, `@sunschool/policy-server`; be the only protection |
| 2 | Layout `(app)` | `requireActiveUser()` — status and roles **from the DB** | trust JWT `status` / `roles` for data access |
| 3 | Route Handlers, Server Actions | `requireActiveUser()` / `requireRole()` as the **first** statement | take `userId` from client input |
| 4 | `@sunschool/policy-server` in DAL | Object-level check: foreign resource → **404**, wrong role → **403** | return a different shape than `MutationResult` |
| 5 | Use-case transaction | Domain rules + write + **audit record in the same transaction** | write audit outside the transaction |

`middleware.ts` is legacy/transitional only — no new gates there.

## Config split (mandatory)

- `auth.config.ts` — edge-safe: providers, `pages`, `authorized`. Imports only `next-auth` and `lib/auth/telegram-oidc-discovery-fetch`.
- `auth.ts` — Node: `NextAuth(...)`, `callbacks`, `handlers`, `auth`, `signIn`, `signOut`; may import `@sunschool/db` and `@sunschool/policy-server`.
- `proxy.ts` imports `auth.config.ts` only.

## JWT and session

- Token holds **only** `uid` (= `app_user.id`, resolved via `login_identity`, **not** the provider's id), `status`, `roles`.
- **No** full name, email, phone or Telegram username in the JWT or in `session.user` (ADR-003 §4.3).
- `jwt` callback does not hit the DB on every request; the token is an optimistic slice. Authoritative status and roles — `requireActiveUser()` per request, cached for **one request** with `React.cache`, never `'use cache'` for user data.
- Session typing — Auth.js module augmentation **only in `apps/web`**; map session → `PolicySessionContext` before `policy-server` ([typescript-monorepo-types.mdc](typescript-monorepo-types.mdc)).
- `redirect` callback: relative paths from `canonical_routes.md` only; external `callbackUrl` is ignored (open redirect).

## Telegram (TG-1…TG-5)

- Sign-in and linking — **client** `signIn("telegram")` from `next-auth/react`; **never** server-side `signIn()` from a Server Action.
- Route handler wraps **both** `GET` and `POST` to shorten `state` to ≤ 256 characters; rewrite error → 500 without details.
- `customFetch` is imported from `next-auth` (same package as `NextAuth`); synthetic `userinfo_endpoint`; `profile().email = null`; `allowDangerousEmailAccountLinking: false`.
- No `AUTH_REDIRECT_PROXY_URL` / `redirectProxyUrl`. Pin `next-auth` and `@auth/core` to exact versions; upgrade as a separate task with the TG-5 acceptance test.
- `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` is not used as `clientSecret`; use `AUTH_TELEGRAM_ID` / `AUTH_TELEGRAM_SECRET`.

## Credentials (administrator) and Telegram profile data

- `authorize()` lives in `auth.ts` (Node, DB); `auth.config.ts` stays edge-safe. Hash = **scrypt** (`node:crypto`), compare with `timingSafeEqual`; 5 failures → 15-minute lock (`failed_attempts`, `locked_until`); same answer for a wrong email and a wrong password.
- The first admin is created by `db:seed:admin` (`FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD` — dev: `.local/dev-secrets.json`, prod: operator env, never Vercel runtime). The app never reads these variables.
- Never log, audit, return or send to Sentry a password, a hash, a phone or a Telegram username (INV-23). Telegram OIDC scope is `openid` only — the app stores `provider_account_id` (`sub`), not Telegram profile or phone fields (ADR-003 v1.2).

## Errors

- Login failures go to `/login?error=<code>`; messages come from the `auth` dictionary slice (`@/lib/messages`), without tokens or other users' data.
- Mutation codes use the `AUTH_` prefix from `@sunschool/domain` (e.g. `AUTH_LINK_CONFLICT`, `AUTH_LAST_IDENTITY`) — no inline strings ([domain-literals-and-codes.mdc](domain-literals-and-codes.mdc)).
- Auth.js swallows OIDC exceptions: log through the `logger` in config so Sentry receives them.

## Do not

- Extend Credentials beyond administrators, add self-registration by password, password reset in the app, Google, or `@auth/prisma-adapter` without amending ADR-001 and ADR-003.
- Put personal data or extra roles into the JWT "for convenience".
- Cache authorization results across requests.
- Log `providerAccountId`, tokens, `AUTH_SECRET` or the link-intent cookie value (INV-23).
- Merge users automatically when an identity belongs to another user — refuse with a code; merging is an admin contract operation.

## Checklist

- [ ] Route protection by prefix in **`proxy.ts`**; **no** `policy-server` / `@sunschool/db` import there
- [ ] Every mutation and protected read calls `requireActiveUser()` before touching data; `userId` only from the session
- [ ] First `ADMIN` created once by `db:seed:admin` (advisory lock, idempotent); password stored as scrypt hash only
- [ ] No password / hash / phone / username in JWT, audit values, logs or Sentry events
- [ ] Link / unlink: idempotent success, conflict code, last identity cannot be removed, `SELECT … FOR UPDATE`
- [ ] Telegram: `state.length ≤ 256`, client `signIn`, both handler methods wrapped
- [ ] Audit record written in the same transaction as the mutation
- [ ] XSS/CSRF/CSP — **security-xss-csrf** + [`ai_security_xss_csrf_guidelines.md`](docs/guidelines/security/ai_security_xss_csrf_guidelines.md)

